Chapter: FsOpsComputedScope
  cites Foreword chapter FileSystem

 A grant over "OPS" binds append-file, make-dir and list-dir as it binds
 write-file and read-text, through their rows in the type checker's
 scoped-op-effect: a literal path is checked against the grant, and a path
 the checker cannot see is refused. Here each op is given one of each, a
 literal outside "OPS" and a computed path, and all six are refused
 (CDX4002). fs-ops is the other half: literal paths inside the grant
 compile and run, which without those rows they did not (every call was
 refused as having no scope of its own).

Section: Paths The Checker Cannot See

  outside : Integer -> Text
  outside (n) = "ELSE" & show n & ".TXT"

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, FileSystem.Read "OPS", FileSystem.Write "OPS"] Nothing
  opening = act
    a <- append-file "ELSE.TXT" "no"
    b <- make-dir "ELSE"
    c <- list-dir "ELSE"
    d <- append-file (outside 0) "no"
    e <- make-dir (outside 1)
    f <- list-dir (outside 2)
    print-line-uni (show a & show b & show (list-length c) & show d & show e & show (list-length f))
  end
